   "text": "This is stanozolol, a 17\u03b1-methyl-17\u03b2-hydroxy androstane steroid with a pyrazole fused to the A ring.\n\n- **Pyrazole ring:** it has an N= at the top, bonded to a CH=, and an NH at the bottom. The NH sits on the carbon next to the CH2 that links to C5, and the CH= sits on the carbon next to the CH2 that links to C10.\n- **D ring:** it carries a tertiary carbon with OH and a hashed methyl, which gives 17\u03b1-methyl and 17\u03b2-OH.\n- **Methyl groups:** there is a wedged methyl at C13 and a wedged methyl at C10.\n- **Ring-fusion hydrogens:** the H atoms at the ring fusions are drawn with wedges or hashes in the standard steroid arrangement.\n\nI wrote the stereocentres from my recollection of the known stanozolol SMILES and only partly checked them against the wedges and hashes in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C[C@]12CC[C@H]3[C@H]([C@@H]1CC[C@]2(C)O)CC[C@@H]4[C@@]3(Cc5c(C4)[nH]nc5)C"
